Z||000003||artherd||08-29-2001||02:47 PM||||I have had my (stock) Formula up to 125. units not specified  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (but I live in CA, do the math.)<P>In 5th gear, redline on my V6 occurs at almost exactly 180mph indicated. One-Eighty. Yes.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||Old Lar||08-29-2001||03:55 PM||||Artherd is correct, if I calculate out top speed and red line in 5th gear it works out to 180 mph.  Somehow my stock doesn't have the ponies to get to redline in 5th or 4th. I have been to 90 in 3rd.  My speedometer only goes to 120, been there, done that. A long straight away.<P>If I do the same math with my 3.4L  OD 4 speed automatic and a 6000 rpm red line, top speed calculates to 230 mph. (25-2600 rpm at 100 mph) I don't think it has the ponies to get to redline either.||||reg||1
